language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Choose as few vertices as possible so that every edge has at least one chosen end.
given n : int(1..100)
given m : int(1..1000)
given edges : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..2)] of int(1..n)
find chosen : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool
find size : int(0..n)
minimising size
such that
$ size counts the chosen vertices
size = sum(chosen),
$ every edge has a chosen end
forAll e : int(1..m) . chosen[edges[e, 1]] \/ chosen[edges[e, 2]]
